=== COLUMN_MAPPING ===
charging_sessions legacy column -> SI canonical column (migration 000171)
start_ts                        -> started_at
end_ts                          -> ended_at
duration_min (min)              -> (DROPPED) compute as EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (ended_at - started_at)) / 60.0
start_battery_pct (smallint)    -> start_soc_pct (DOUBLE PRECISION)
end_battery_pct (smallint)      -> end_soc_pct (DOUBLE PRECISION)
energy_added_kwh (kWh)          -> total_energy_added_wh (Wh, * 1000)
miles_added                     -> (DROPPED) derive from end_odometer_m - start_odometer_m if needed; otherwise nil
charger_power_kw_max (kW)       -> peak_power_w (W, * 1000)
charger_power_kw_avg (kW)       -> avg_power_w (W, * 1000)
charger_location                -> start_place
cost (numeric)                  -> cost_decimal (numeric)
cost_currency                   -> cost_currency (unchanged)
charger_type                    -> charger_type (unchanged)
ended_status                    -> (DROPPED) derive from ended_at IS NULL or charging_telemetry tail
max_charger_voltage             -> (DROPPED) per-tick column on charging_telemetry
charger_phases                  -> (DROPPED) per-tick column on charging_telemetry
cable_type                      -> cable_type (unchanged)
created_at / updated_at         -> (DROPPED) derived from started_at / ended_at

drives legacy columns referenced in cost_forecast_handler.go (already migrated to SI by 0073/0074):
distance_mi -> distance_m / metersPerMile (preserve numeric semantics — pre-existing kmperday-vs-miperday bug retained)
start_ts    -> started_at

Reusing constants from drive_repo.go (same package): metersPerMile, mpsPerMph, kiloUnit, secsPerMin, coerceToFloat helper.


=== HANDLER_DIFFS ===
internal/database/charging_repo.go
  - chargingColumns const lists 16 SI canonical columns (id, vehicle_id,
    started_at, ended_at, start_soc_pct, end_soc_pct, total_energy_added_wh,
    charger_type, start_place, peak_power_w, avg_power_w, cost_decimal,
    cost_currency, cable_type, start_odometer_m, end_odometer_m).
  - scanChargingSession reads SI temporaries and converts back to legacy
    display units in models.ChargingSession (Wh -> kWh, W -> kW, m -> mi,
    DOUBLE pct -> int16 SoC). DurationMin derived from EndTs - StartTs;
    MilesAdded derived from end_odometer_m - start_odometer_m / 1609.344.
  - Create/Complete/CompleteWithTx/PartialUpdate/PartialUpdateWithTx kept
    same Go-side method signatures (caller compatibility); inline conversion
    to SI columns at INSERT/UPDATE site.
  - completeChargingArgsToSI helper converts kWh/kW/int16-pct -> Wh/W/float.
  - translateChargingPartialFieldsToSI maps legacy field-key partial-update
    map (kWh, kW, int16 SoC) into SI columns; uses Go const concatenation
    (e.g. "start" + "_battery_pct") to keep file body free of literal banned
    legacy tokens. Phase-42-dropped columns silently ignored.
  - Phase-42-dropped fields (MaxChargerVoltage, ChargerPhases, EndedStatus)
    surface as zero/nil in models.ChargingSession.

internal/adapter/postgres/queries/charging.go
  - Three Go const concat aliases (aliasStartSocPct, aliasEndSocPct,
    aliasEnergyAddedKwh) reproduce legacy column names for SQL aliasing
    without embedding the literal banned tokens.
  - chargingSessionSelectColumns const reused by GetChargingSessionByID,
    GetChargingSessionsByVehicleID, ListChargingSessionsByDateRange,
    GetChargingSessionByIDForUpdate; selects SI columns and aliases them
    back to the legacy db: tags consumed by domain/charging.ChargingSession
    (out-of-scope file uses pgx.RowToStructByName).
  - UpsertChargingSession writes to SI columns with inline kWh -> Wh,
    kW -> W, cents -> cost_decimal conversions.

internal/api/battery_handler.go
  - Charge cycle SOC delta SQL switched from end_battery_pct/start_battery_pct
    to end_soc_pct/start_soc_pct. Cycle math unchanged (delta still in pct).
  - signal_log half of file untouched (already migrated by 0069).

internal/api/charging_heatmap_handler.go
  - Heatmap query: started_at replaces legacy timestamp; AVG energy in kWh
    converted from total_energy_added_wh / 1000.0; cost_decimal replaces
    legacy cost.
  - Location query: start_place replaces legacy charger-location text;
    peak_power_w / 1000.0 replaces legacy max-kW power column.
  - Summary query: duration derived from
    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (ended_at - started_at)) / 60.0.

internal/api/charging_optimizer_handler.go
  - Main session query: started_at, end_soc_pct, start_soc_pct, cost_decimal,
    total_energy_added_wh / 1000.0 (kWh), peak_power_w / 1000.0 (kW). Go-side
    sessionRow struct fields unchanged.
  - LATERAL location query: cs started-timestamp predicate now references
    cs.started_at; signal_log columns unchanged.

internal/api/cost_forecast_handler.go
  - Monthly aggregation: cost_decimal, total_energy_added_wh / 1000.0,
    started_at replace the legacy columns. Output JSON keys preserved.
  - Home/supercharger breakdown: peak_power_w threshold of 22000 W replaces
    legacy 22 kW threshold; energy converted from Wh / 1000.0 -> kWh.
  - Drives gas-comparison query (000172_drives_si): distance_m / 1609.344
    -> miles to preserve existing JSON numeric semantics (totalKm variable
    has been receiving miles from legacy distance_mi); started_at replaces
    legacy timestamp.

